Insert resume watchdog state after `switchFailed`. Also `holding` doc change. Add:
```ts
/** This binding's token in the process-wide want set. */
const gateToken = Symbol("peak-gate");
let wantsGate = false;
let disposed = false;
let timerCtx: ExtensionContext | undefined;
let sessionId: string | undefined;
let sessionCwd: string | undefined;
let isMainSession = false;
let runActive = false;
let runSawPause = false;
let pausedWithQueue = false;
let gateHeldAt: number | undefined;
let resumePending = false;
let resumeReason: string | undefined;
let resumeTimer: Timer | undefined;
let waitTimer: Timer | undefined;
let resumeAttempts = 0;
let activeWait: { id: string; startedAt: number } | undefined;
const interruptedWaits = new Set<string>();
```

Add functions after `holdProcess`:
- `setGateWant(want)`.
- `cancelResumeTimer`, `cancelWaitTimer`.
- `writeMarkerIfMain`.
- `scheduleResumeCheck`, `attemptResume`.
- `scheduleWaitInterrupt`.
- `handleGateClosed`, `handleGateOpened`.
- `initSession`.
But some functions reference `context`, `pi`, etc.

Order: functions can be declared as consts before use (TDZ) as long as not called during initialization. `apply` is defined later; fine.

`setGateWant`:
```ts
const setGateWant = (want: boolean): void => {
  if (disposed) return;
  if (want === wantsGate) { syncPeakGate(); return; } // still sync so a user /resume is re-closed
  wantsGate = want;
  if (want) gateWanters.add(gateToken); else gateWanters.delete(gateToken);
  syncPeakGate();
};
```
Note: calling syncPeakGate even when unchanged re-pauses after user resume, preserving current behavior.

`dropGateWant` on shutdown: `if (wantsGate) { wantsGate=false; gateWanters.delete(gateToken); syncPeakGate(); }`.

`writeMarkerIfMain`:
```ts
const writeMarkerIfMain = (): void => {
  if (!RESUME_ENABLED || !isMainSession || sessionId === undefined || sessionCwd === undefined) return;
  writeResumeMarker(sessionId, sessionCwd);
};
```

`cancelResumeTimer`:
```ts
const cancelResumeTimer = (): void => {
  if (resumeTimer !== undefined) { try { (timerCtx ?? context)?.clearTimer(resumeTimer); } catch {} resumeTimer = undefined; }
};
```
`cancelWaitTimer` similar.

`apply` uses `holdProcess(holding || resumePending)`. If resumePending and gate closes, keepalive stays; fine.

`scheduleResumeCheck`:
```ts
const scheduleResumeCheck = (reason: string): void => {
  if (!RESUME_ENABLED || disposed || !isMainSession || context === undefined) return;
  resumePending = true;
  resumeReason = reason;
  if (resumeTimer !== undefined) return;
  const c = context;
  resumeTimer = c.setTimeout(() => { resumeTimer = undefined; attemptResume(); }, RESUME_GRACE_MS);
  holdProcess(true);
};
```
`holdProcess(true)` even if holding false; okay. On attempt, recalc.

`attemptResume`:
```ts
const attemptResume = (): void => {
  const c = context;
  if (!RESUME_ENABLED || disposed || !isMainSession || c === undefined) return;
  if (agentPauseGate.paused) { holdProcess(holding); return; } // re-armed by next open
  if (!c.isIdle()) {
    if (activeWait !== undefined) scheduleWaitInterrupt(activeWait.id);
    holdProcess(holding);
    return;
  }
  if (c.getAsyncJobSnapshot()?.running.length) { holdProcess(holding); return; }
  if (resumeAttempts >= MAX_RESUMES_PER_HOLD) { resumePending=false; clearResumeMarker(); holdProcess(holding); return; }
  resumeAttempts++;
  try {
    pi.sendUserMessage(RESUME_PROMPT, { attribution: "agent" });
  } catch (error) { debug; c.ui.notify warning; }
  debug(`resume: injected continuation (${resumeReason ?? "unknown"})`);
  c.ui.notify("Peak gate released: resuming the interrupted turn", "info");
  resumePending = false; resumeReason = undefined;
  clearResumeMarker();
  holdProcess(holding);
};
```
Question: `c.isIdle()` false at the grace but the loop is parked at the *gate*? No, gate open. It should be running. If false because the run is inside a wait, schedule interrupt.
`hasPendingMessages` is fine either way; `sendUserMessage` starts a turn and the queued messages deliver with it. But if the session is idle with pending *followUp* messages, sending a prompt starts a turn; okay.

If `sendUserMessage` throws, should we keep `resumePending` for a retry? Don't loop. Clear and notify.

`scheduleWaitInterrupt`:
```ts
const scheduleWaitInterrupt = (waitId: string): void => {
  if (!RESUME_ENABLED || disposed || waitTimer !== undefined || interruptedWaits.has(waitId)) return;
  const c = context; if (c === undefined) return;
  waitTimer = c.setTimeout(() => {
    waitTimer = undefined;
    if (disposed || context === undefined || agentPauseGate.paused) return;
    if (activeWait?.id !== waitId || interruptedWaits.has(waitId)) return;
    if (context.isIdle()) { scheduleResumeCheck("wait-ended"); return; }
    if (context.hasPendingMessages()) return; // a queued steer already cuts the wait
    interruptedWaits.add(waitId);
    try { pi.sendUserMessage(WAIT_RESUME_PROMPT, { deliverAs: "aside", attribution: "agent" }); } catch (e) { debug; return; }
    debug("resume: interrupted an in-flight wait after gate release");
    context.ui.notify("Peak gate released: interrupting the pending wait so the turn continues", "info");
  }, WAIT_INTERRUPT_DELAY_MS);
};
```
But `scheduleWaitInterrupt` is called from `attemptResume` when busy, and from `handleGateOpened`. Need to gate on hold duration: `gateHeldAt` is cleared on open. Store `lastHoldEndedAt`/`lastHoldDuration`. In `handleGateOpened`, compute `heldFor` and pass a boolean `allowWaitInterrupt` to a variable `waitInterruptEligible = heldFor >= WAIT_INTERRUPT_MIN_HOLD_MS`. `attemptResume` may be called later; use the variable until the next gate close. Set `waitInterruptEligible=false` on gate close. Then `scheduleWaitInterrupt` checks it.
Also ensure the wait was active during the hold: `activeWait.startedAt <= gateOpenedAt`. Store `gateOpenedAt = Date.now()`; pass:
```ts
const waitIsGateRelated = activeWait !== undefined && activeWait.startedAt <= gateOpenedAt
```
If the wait started after release, no. In `attemptResume`, if busy with a wait that started after open, don't interrupt.

`handleGateClosed`:
```ts
const handleGateClosed = (): void => {
  if (disposed || !isMainSession) return;
  gateHeldAt ??= Date.now();
  waitInterruptEligible = false;
  resumeAttempts = 0;
  if (runActive) { runSawPause = true; writeMarkerIfMain(); }
  if (context?.hasPendingMessages()) { pausedWithQueue = true; writeMarkerIfMain(); }
};
```
Note: if the gate closes due to the fallback path, `runActive` true → marker written, then fallback resumes quickly → on open, `runActive && !idle` → clear marker. Fine.

`handleGateOpened`:
```ts
const handleGateOpened = (): void => {
  if (disposed || !isMainSession || context === undefined) return;
  const now = Date.now();
  const heldFor = gateHeldAt === undefined ? 0 : now - gateHeldAt;
  gateHeldAt = undefined;
  gateOpenedAt = now;
  waitInterruptEligible = heldFor >= WAIT_INTERRUPT_MIN_HOLD_MS;
  const c = context;
  if (resumePending) { scheduleResumeCheck(resumeReason ?? "gate-released"); return; }
  if (pausedWithQueue) {
    pausedWithQueue = false;
    if (c.isIdle() && c.hasPendingMessages()) { scheduleResumeCheck("queued-work"); return; }
  }
  if (runActive && !c.isIdle()) {
    // A parked loop woke and owns the session; a stale marker must not fire later.
    clearResumeMarker();
    if (waitInterruptEligible && activeWait !== undefined && activeWait.startedAt <= now) scheduleWaitInterrupt(activeWait.id);
    return;
  }
  if (c.isIdle()) {
    clearResumeMarker();
    // A gate hold that produced no resumable work leaves nothing to do.
    if (resumePending) scheduleResumeCheck(resumeReason ?? "gate-released");
  }
};
```
Hmm the last `if (resumePending)` is unreachable because we returned earlier. Remove.
What if `runActive` true but `isIdle()` true (run ended but agent_end not yet dispatched)? `agent_end` will handle. On open, neither branch; leave marker? We shouldn't clear; the agent_end handler will set pending or clear. But if the run ended normally, agent_end clears. Fine. Don't clear in that limbo.
What if `runActive` false and `isIdle` false? Odd; leave.
`pausedWithQueue` should be reset at open regardless after check. Also reset if not idle? If a run is active with queued messages, the run will consume them; clear the flag.
Set `pausedWithQueue=false` at top after capturing.

`initSession(ctx)`:
```ts
const initSession = (ctx: ExtensionContext): void => {
  sessionId = ctx.sessionManager.getSessionId();
  sessionCwd = ctx.cwd;
  isMainSession = ctx.agent.kind === "main";
  runActive = false; runSawPause = false; pausedWithQueue = false; gateHeldAt = undefined;
  resumePending = false; resumeReason = undefined; resumeAttempts = 0; activeWait = undefined;
  cancelResumeTimer(); cancelWaitTimer();
  if (!isMainSession || !RESUME_ENABLED) return;
  const marker = readResumeMarker();
  if (marker !== undefined && marker.sessionId === sessionId && (marker.cwd === undefined || marker.cwd === sessionCwd)) {
    resumePending = true; resumeReason = "restart";
    debug(`resume: marker found for session ${sessionId} (age ${Math.round((Date.now()-marker.at)/1000)}s)`);
    if (!agentPauseGate.paused) scheduleResumeCheck("restart");
  }
};
```
